  "version": "1.1.0",
  "kind": "standard",
  "organization": "ScaleDock",
  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers IETF HTTP Semantics (RFC 9110) and HTTP Caching (RFC 9111) for API and server authors: method safety and idempotency, status codes, validators and conditional requests (ETag, If-Match, If-None-Match, 304, 412), content negotiation and Vary, range requests, and Cache-Control freshness and validation, plus the RFC 5861 stale extensions. It also covers the HTTP extension fields APIs use most: the QUERY method (RFC 10008), Structured Field Values (RFC 9651), Web Linking (RFC 8288), Deprecation (RFC 9745), Sunset (RFC 8594), api-catalog (RFC 9727), Prefer (RFC 7240), and tracks the expired Idempotency-Key draft-07. Legacy lines RFC 7230-7235 and RFC 8941 are read and upgraded from. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions and upgrades, methods and status codes, conditional and range requests, caching and negotiation, structured fields, and the API lifecycle fields. Also covers Alt-Svc, Early Hints, Client Hints, Cache-Status, Proxy-Status, Targeted Cache-Control, Priority, PATCH, multipart/form-data, Link-Template and Compression Dictionary Transport, and tracks Resumable Uploads draft-12.",
